@startuml
title Janus — email-confirmed signup and asynchronous account creation
actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Auth Lambda" as Auth
participant "Amazon Cognito" as Cognito
participant "PostConfirmation Lambda" as Confirmed
queue "SQS account queue" as Queue
participant "Provision Lambda" as Provision
participant "Account HTTP Lambda" as AccountRead
database "Account DynamoDB" as DB

Client -> Gateway: POST /signup (API key)
Gateway -> Auth: invoke
Auth -> Cognito: SignUp (email and password)
Cognito --> Client: Email confirmation code (via Cognito)
Auth --> Gateway: Confirmation required
Gateway --> Client: Confirmation pending

Client -> Gateway: POST /confirm (email and code, API key)
Gateway -> Auth: invoke
Auth -> Cognito: ConfirmSignUp (email and code)
Cognito -> Confirmed: PostConfirmation_ConfirmSignUp\nverified userAttributes
Confirmed -> Queue: Send account event (sub + email)
Confirmed --> Cognito: Return event
Cognito --> Auth: Confirmation complete
Auth --> Gateway: Success
Gateway --> Client: Confirmation complete

Queue -> Provision: Deliver (at least once)
Provision -> DB: PutItem if id does not exist
DB --> Provision: Created or already exists

note over Cognito, DB
Confirm and queue enqueue are not atomic.
Failure recovery and DLQ reconciliation require AWS integration tests.
end note

Client -> Gateway: GET /account (API key + ID token)
Gateway -> Gateway: Cognito authorizer verifies token
Gateway -> AccountRead: Claims with verified sub
AccountRead -> DB: GetItem(id = sub)
DB --> AccountRead: Account
AccountRead --> Gateway: Response
Gateway --> Client: Account
@enduml
